  ('guanajuato-city-mexico', '10S', 'Guanajuato City', 'Mexico', 'A city that sings', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Guanajuato (San Miguel de Allende)', '{"romance","culture","entertainment","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["UNESCO World Heritage (inscribed 1988) — colonial mining-town ensemble; one of the world''s richest colonial silver sources (Source: machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-05)","Callejoneada: estudiantina in Renaissance costume leads roving alley serenades with wine + candies (Source: en.wikipedia.org, Accessed 2026-07-05)","Festival Internacional Cervantino, Mexico''s largest performing-arts festival, Oct 7–25 2026 — sells out months ahead (Source: planetamericas.com, Accessed 2026-07-05)","Museo de las Momias displays 111 naturally mummified bodies exhumed 1865–1958 (Source: mexicotravelandleisure.com, Accessed 2026-07-05)","Diego Rivera born 1886 in the Calle Pocitos house, now a museum; ~2,000 m altitude; BJX ~30–40 min (Source: mexicotravelandleisure.com / en.wikipedia.org, Accessed 2026-07-05)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Guanajuato City private clinics + general hospital for routine/stabilization; advanced trauma/cardiac evac to León (~30–40 min, tertiary hub) — confirm in-city facility at booking","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"BJX (Del Bajío/León, ~30–40 min)","stay_in_zone_advisory":"Stay in the compact historic-center tourist zone; risk is rural/highway south of Federal Hwy 45D (Celaya/Salamanca/Irapuato industrial-oil-theft corridor), not the callejones; do not self-drive southern-Guanajuato highways; use vetted transfers","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","altitude":"~2,000 m (~6,600 ft) — mild AMS possible day 1–2; very steep/stepped city; hydrate, pace alcohol","water":"bottled/purified only","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":