  ('hopkins-belize', '10S', 'Hopkins', 'Belize', 'Garifuna drums and the southern reef', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Belize', '{"tropical","expedition","culture"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["The Garifuna cultural heart of Belize — living drumming tradition (Lebeha Drumming Center, est. 2002) and cuisine that is UNESCO-recognized intangible heritage (proclaimed 2001).","Gateway to Cockscomb Basin Wildlife Sanctuary — 128,000 acres, established 1986 as the world''s first jaguar preserve; ~200 jaguars and ~290 bird species.","One of the only places in Belize where the barrier reef and the rainforest are reachable from the same beach; South Water Caye is among the least-dived, healthiest reef systems in the country.","Mayflower Bocawina National Park (12 mi inland) has Belize''s longest zipline (2.5 mi) and its only guided waterfall rappel (Antelope Falls, 250 ft).","Garifuna Settlement Day (Nov 19) — Hopkins is one of three national epicenters, with a dawn Yurumein landing re-enactment and all-night drumming."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police & ambulance); maritime VHF Ch 16 or 966 — verify locally","hospital":"Dangriga (Southern Regional Hospital) for town care; serious trauma routes to Belize City; international medical evacuation the realistic path for major injury","recompression_chamber":"Ambergris Caye / San Pedro (24/7, tel 226-2660; DAN +1-919-684-9111) — FAR from Hopkins; dive conservatively","advisory_date":"2026-06-18","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) only","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on TWW''s BOOK WITH WARNING (Four-Bin v3) posture — full-advisory disclosure + traveler acknowledgment at booking; only Southside Belize City is named, away from Hopkins","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE (Philip Goldson Intl) -> Dangriga/Hopkins DGA via Tropic Air/Maya Island Air (~25 min flight) + ~40 min drive; or ~2.5 hr direct drive from BZE","malaria":"WHO-certified malaria-free 2023; low localized inland risk only; dengue is an active 2026 risk (2,794 cases in 2025); jungle excursions raise mosquito exposure","water":"treat/bottled outside resorts","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belize","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:57Z","page_updated":"2026-06-12T10:40:30+01:00","source_country":"belize","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","dive_emergency_numbers_verified":{"read":"2026-08-30","numbers":{"+1-919-684-9111":"DAN 24/7 emergency hotline — dan.org/about-dan/contact/, read 2026-08-30","226-2660":"Belize Chamber Project, San Pedro, 24/7 — sanpedrosun.com / ambergriscaye.com, read 2026-08-30"},"_rule":"Each number above was read from the authority named beside it on the date shown. ⛔ A number with no entry here has NOT been verified and must not be presented as an emergency contact."}},"timing":{"peak_dry":"late-December to April","green_value_season":"June to November (30-40% savings)","event_peak":"Garifuna Settlement Day, November 19","secondary_events":["Hopkins Day (July)","Independence Day (September)"],"curve_start_dry":"mid-October","curve_start_event":"early-October","fire_date":"late-September to early-October","confidence":"seasonal-pattern-derived; sharpen on live booking pace"},"jewels":[{"name":"Lebeha Drumming Center","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lebeha_Drumming_Center","si":"culture","commission":"cultural experience add-on / direct-book","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Warasa Garifuna Drum School (Punta Gorda)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.warasadrumschool.com/","si":"culture","commission":"cultural add-on","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Garifuna cuisine (hudut/sere/ereba) cooking class","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://belizenewspost.com/garifuna-food/","si":"culture","commission":"culinary experience / homestay bundle","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Garifuna Settlement Day (Nov 19)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://caribbeanlifestyle.com/garifuna-settlement-day-belize/","hook":"November 19 The single sharpest cultural spike of the year: dawn Yurumein re-enactment, all-night drumming, parades. Hopkins is one of three epicenters","si":"culture","blurb":"November 19 The single sharpest cultural spike of the year: dawn Yurumein re-enactment, all-night drumming, parades. Hopkins is one of three epicenters","commission":"event-anchored stay+culture package","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["package","event"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Cockscomb Basin Wildlife Sanctuary (world''s first jaguar preserve)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockscomb_Basin_Wildlife_Sanctuary","hook":"Established 1986, it holds ~200 jaguars plus puma, ocelot and ~290 bird species, reachable as a day trip rather than an expedition","si":"expedition","blurb":"Established 1986, it holds ~200 jaguars plus puma, ocelot and ~290 bird species, reachable as a day trip rather than an expedition","commission":"guided day-tour (gate non-commissionable)","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Mayflower Bocawina National Park (waterfalls/zipline/rappel)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.islandexpeditions.com/belize-vacations-blog/5-ways-explore-mayflower-bocawina-national-park","si":"expedition","commission":"full-day adventure operator","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Sittee River manatee & birding","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.magnumbelize.com/tours-2/sittee-river-kayaking/","hook":"Guided motorboat/kayak; crocodiles present — stay in the vessel, follow guide, no swimming in river sections. Manatees are protected — no-touch, no-chase","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided motorboat/kayak; crocodiles present — stay in the vessel, follow guide, no swimming in river sections. Manatees are protected — no-touch, no-chase","commission":"half-day adventure operator","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"South Water Caye Marine Reserve + Glover''s Reef","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.zubludiving.com/destination/belize/stan-creek-district/hopkins-placencia-glovers-reef","si":"tropical","commission":"dive own CLIA lane; snorkel day-trip operators","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","tropical":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What makes Hopkins different from Belize''s other beach spots?","a":"It is a rare double-header: one of the very few points on the Caribbean where the barrier reef and the rainforest are visible from the same beach chair, on a 12-mile beach. Because the southern barrier reef here fronts a low-population mainland, South Water Caye Marine Reserve is one of the least-dived, healthiest reef systems in the country.","source":"hamanasi.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Can you visit the jaguar preserve from Hopkins?","a":"Yes — Cockscomb Basin, the world''s first jaguar preserve (128,000 acres, est. 1986), is about 30–40 minutes inland and works as a day trip, from an hour-long river stroll to a four-day Victoria Peak trek. The BZ$10 non-national entry fee is government pass-through; you book the guided day-tour for the value.","source":"hamanasi.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Hopkins a good honeymoon destination?","a":"Yes, for jungle-and-reef romance rather than resort glitz. Hamanasi — a Tripadvisor Top-25-in-world honoree with 30 treehouse/beachfront rooms, a PADI facility and Green Globe certification — plus Belizean Dreams and Jaguar Reef Lodge are built around couples with private-guide adventures and infinity pools.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Why is Hopkins the Garifuna cultural heart of Belize?","a":"Daily drum schools, homestays and food workshops make Hopkins the single most accessible stop to experience living Garifuna heritage — itself UNESCO-recognized intangible heritage (proclaimed 2001). Garifuna Settlement Day on November 19 brings a dawn Yurumein re-enactment and all-night drumming, and rooms in the village sell out.","source":"belizenewspost.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Hopkins?","a":"Medical remoteness and mosquitoes, not crime. the nearest hospital is Dangriga, with trauma routing to Belize City. Dengue is an active 2026 risk (2,794 cases in 2025), and jungle excursions raise exposure.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belize","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Mayflower Bocawina waterfall rappel or the jungle hiking dangerous?","a":"Mayflower Bocawina holds Belize''s longest zipline (2.5 mi) and its only guided waterfall rappel (Antelope Falls, 250 ft) — certified guides and provided harness/helmet only, never solo. In Cockscomb, the Tiger Fern Trail now requires a guide (mandated after a hiker fatality) and Victoria Peak (3,675 ft) is dry-season-only and guide-mandatory.","source":"mayflowerbocawina.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Hopkins, Belize: Garifuna Culture, Jaguar Preserve & Reef Travel Guide (2026)","meta_description":"Hopkins is Belize''s Garifuna cultural heart — drumming, uncrowded beach, gateway to Cockscomb Basin jaguar preserve, Mayflower Bocawina waterfalls, and the southern barrier reef.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Hopkins Belize Garifuna drumming","Cockscomb Basin jaguar preserve tour from Hopkins","Hopkins Belize diving South Water Caye","Mayflower Bocawina waterfall rappel zipline","Sittee River manatee tour Belize","Garifuna Settlement Day Hopkins November 19","best time to visit Hopkins Belize","Hamanasi vs Belizean Dreams Hopkins","Hopkins Belize beach villa rental","is Hopkins Belize safe 2026","hudut Garifuna food Hopkins"],"hreflang":["en"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-06","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/belize","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:57Z","source_updated":"2026-06-12T10:40:30+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["tropical","expedition","culture"],"ultra":[{"name":"Hamanasi Adventure & Dive Resort","location":"Hopkins","tier":"$$$$ premier","lane":"Fora/AOR · MoR","note":"Tripadvisor Top-25-in-world honoree; treehouses; Green Globe"},{"name":"Itz''ana Resort & Residences","location":"Placencia (~45-60 min south)","tier":"$$$$ ultra","lane":"Fora/AOR · MoR","note":"nearest true ultra; SLH / MICHELIN Guide; villas + marina"},{"name":"Naïa Resort & Spa","location":"Placencia","tier":"$$$$ ultra","lane":"Fora/AOR","note":"ultra beachfront spa/villa"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Hopkins, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":16.105,"lng":-88.2867},"orbit":[{"id":"ambergris-caye-belize","jewels":11,"si":["tropical","liveaboard","romance","expedition"]},{"id":"blue-hole-belize","jewels":8,"si":["liveaboard","expedition","tropical"]},{"id":"caye-caulker-belize","jewels":9,"si":["tropical","liveaboard","expedition","ocean","culinary"]},{"id":"placencia-belize","jewels":8,"si":["liveaboard","expedition","diveglobal","ocean","wildlife","culture"]},{"id":"san-ignacio-belize","jewels":13,"si":["expedition","culture","romance"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 47),
  ('huatulco-mexico', '10S', 'Huatulco', 'Mexico', 'Oaxaca''s calm nine-bay coast', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Oaxaca (Oaxaca City & Coast)', '{"expedition","diveglobal","ocean","culture","wildlife","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Nine bays across 36 beaches; horseshoe coves stay calm for swimming/snorkeling — greener and calmer than surf-driven Puerto Escondido.","Huatulco National Park protects ~11,890 ha of coast, reef and forest; dolphins, turtles and seasonal whales.","Playa La Entrega is the best land-accessible snorkel cove — reef starts feet from shore.","Pluma Hidalgo (~1,350 m, 45 min inland) produces some of the Americas'' top high-altitude Arabica coffee.","Copalita is one of only two seaside archaeological sites in Mexico (with Tulum) — Zapotec/Mixtec city settled by ~500 BC.","Humpback whale season Dec 15-Mar 21 (97% sighting success at peak); olive-ridley/green turtle nesting Jul-Jan."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Local Huatulco/La Crucecita clinics stabilize routine cases; serious trauma routes to Oaxaca City or Mexico City for definitive/ICU care","advisory_note":"updated May 29, 2026","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":true,"malaria":"low/negligible in Huatulco tourist coast","dengue":"endemic seasonal risk, higher May-Nov; use repellent","water":"bottled/purified only; resort water filtered","swimming":"calmer/safer bays than Puerto Escondido, but open beaches carry riptides — swim sheltered coves","hurricane_season":"Pacific storm season ~Jun-Oct; insure/refundable","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"MX","summary":"The FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named states, cities and border areas of Mexico — listed below in its own words, each with its own exceptions. The Yucatán Peninsula, Mexico City, Baja California Sur and the other main visitor regions carry no FCDO restriction.","source":"UK FCDO — Mexico travel advice, reviewed 2026-07-16 (verbatim snapshot from the research library)","_r