  ('lake-atitlan-guatemala', '10S', 'Lake Atitlán', 'Guatemala', '*If it''s the first pale light on three volcanoes', 'live', 'verified', 'desertDunes', 'Guatemala', '{"adventure","romance","culture","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Volcanic caldera lake at 1,562 m (5,125 ft), up to 340 m deep, ~130 km², ringed by three volcanoes — San Pedro, Tolimán, Atitlán (Source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Atitlán, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Villages divide by role: Panajachel gateway hub, San Pedro backpacker/Spanish-school, San Marcos yoga/wellness, Santiago Atitlán largest/traditional, San Juan weaving + coffee (Source: adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Indian Nose sunrise hike (~30 min pre-dawn) is the signature caldera overlook; San Marcos offers yoga retreats + Cerro Tzankujil cliff-jump (Source: adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Dry season Nov–Apr is most photogenic; Christmas + Semana Santa fill weeks ahead; Sept–Oct rates 40–50% below peak (Source: atitlan.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)","Air access via GUA (La Aurora Intl) + shuttle/private transfer ~3 hr to Panajachel; boat (lancha) is the only road between villages (Source: theabroadblog.com / adventurouskate.com, Accessed 2026-07-06)"],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police · 122/123 ambulance · 1500 ASISTUR/PROATUR (or +502-2290-2810) — verify locally","hospital":"Panajachel/Sololá clinics + regional hospital for stabilization; serious trauma/cardiac evac to Guatemala City (~3 hr road); highlands lack tertiary trauma capability","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"stay_in_zone":true,"founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on TWW''s BOOK WITH WARNING (Four-Bin v3) framing (same founder/attorney axis as the held Central-Mexico SR6)","air_access_verified":"GUA (La Aurora Intl) + shuttle/private transfer ~3 hr to Panajachel","altitude":"~1,562 m (5,125 ft) lakeside — mild; volcano summits San Pedro ~3,020 m / Atitlán ~3,535 m reach real