eb 8–10); secondary Inti Raymi-season (late June) overflow","inflection_curve_start":"early December (Candelaria) / early April (dry-season core)","fire_date":"mid–late November (Candelaria/Feb) & mid–late March (May–Sep core)","green_offseason":"November–March (minus the February Candelaria spike)","binding_constraint":"Candelaria lodging sellout + acclimatization sequencing; often booked as the Cusco↔Arequipa overland link"},"jewels":[{"name":"Uros floating reed islands","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.theonlyperuguide.com/peru-guide/puno/uros-floating-islands/","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"hand-built totora-reed islands ~30 min by boat from Puno, springy underfoot, where the Uros people still live and build. Real communities","si":"culture","blurb":"hand-built totora-reed islands ~30 min by boat from Puno, springy underfoot, where the Uros people still live and build. Real communities","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC/operator day tour + Uros community landing fee (non-comm) + reed-craft retail","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Taquile Island (UNESCO textile island)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/taquile-and-its-textile-art-00166","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"terraced island where knitting is done by men and weaving by women; the textile art is on UNESCO''s Intangible Cultural Heritage list","si":"culture","blurb":"terraced island where knitting is done by men and weaving by women; the textile art is on UNESCO''s Intangible Cultural Heritage list","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC/operator day or 2-day tour + community entry (non-comm) + textile-cooperative retail","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Amantaní homestay + starry night","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.peroudecouverte.com/peru-puno-amantani-island-homestay-pachamama-en.html","hook":"the deepest cultural time on the lake: overnight with a Quechua family, shared meals, dance in borrowed dress","si":"culture","blurb":"the deepest cultural time on the lake: overnight with a Quechua family, shared meals, dance in borrowed dress","commission":"direct-to-community co-op (thin margin) + homestay/community fee (non-comm)","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Sillustani chullpa towers (sunset)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.machutravelperu.com/blog/puno-sillustani","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"pre-Inca Colla funerary towers up to 12 m tall on a peninsula over Lake Umayo, ~35 km from Puno","si":"culture","blurb":"pre-Inca Colla funerary towers up to 12 m tall on a peninsula over Lake Umayo, ~35 km from Puno","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/operator afternoon excursion + site entry (non-comm)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Virgen de la Candelaria festival (February)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.urosexpeditions.com/travel-news/candelaria-festival-2026-official-schedule-dance-order","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the largest folk-festival gatherings in the Americas: thousands of dancers, \"traje de luces\" sequined costumes, brass bands","si":"culture","blurb":"one of the largest folk-festival gatherings in the Americas: thousands of dancers, \"traje de luces\" sequined costumes, brass bands","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC festival package (hotel + guiding + stadium seating); book by mid–late Nov","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","package","hotel","event"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Llachón peninsula community tourism (Capachica)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://titicacatravel-ip.com/en/tour/lake-titicaca/homestay-tour-llachon-amantani-taquile-islands","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the mainland community-tourism heartland on the Capachica peninsula: experiential homestays, weaving, cooking and sailing with families, quieter than the islands","si":"culture","blurb":"the mainland community-tourism heartland on the Capachica peninsula: experiential homestays, weaving, cooking and sailing with families, quieter than the islands","when":"May–September","commission":"direct-to-community co-op + DMC add-on","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Aymara / Quechua living culture","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sillustani","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the altiplano is a living Aymara–Quechua cultural landscape; language, dress, agriculture and belief are the deep story that ties every island and shore together","si":"culture","blurb":"the altiplano is a living Aymara–Quechua cultural landscape; language, dress, agriculture and belief are the deep story that ties every island and shore together","when":"May–September","commission":"DMC cultural interpretation woven through every tour","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Luxury catamaran day-sail (Peru-side)","si_tag":"GEA / RHN","tier":"comfort","source":"https://titicaca.cruises/en/home/","timing":"May–September","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a private or shared catamaran across the open lake. Outdoor decks, Cordillera views, and — on some operators","si":"expedition","blurb":"a private or shared catamaran across the open lake. Outdoor decks, Cordillera views, and — on some operators","when":"May–September","commission":"lake-operator net/commissionable tour (Peru-side only); private charter highest margin","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["GEA / RHN","expedition","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"GEA / RHN":"evidenced","culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"GEA / RHN","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''GEA / RHN'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"}],"faq":[{"q":"Are the Uros, Taquile and Amantaní islands worth it — and does my money reach the families?","a":"Yes, and this is the reason to come. Booked through the community co-op, an Amantaní overnight homestay costs roughly $10–15 per person including meals and rotates through ten host communities, so the income reaches families directly rather than mainland middlemen — the deepest cultural experience on the lake.","source":"peroudecouverte.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How hard is the island walking, and what should I plan for?","a":"Plan for altitude, not difficulty. Island hikes run ~3,800–4,100 m — Taquile is a steady 30–60 minute uphill from the dock, and Amantaní''s twin temple hills top near 4,100 m — so the real risk is AMS. Arrive already acclimatized, pace the climb, and carry water.","source":"bushop.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Lake Titicaca good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, as a quiet luxe add-on to a Cusco/Machu Picchu core. The standout is Titilaka, an 18-suite all-inclusive Relais & Châteaux lodge on a private peninsula with lake-view suites, a private jetty and oxygen-quiet calm — sunrise over the water and private catamaran sailing.","source":"relaischateaux.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Altitude — full stop. At ~3,810 m the lake is the highest stop on most Peru circuits, higher than Cusco, so AMS (soroche) is the dominant safety fact and outranks crime by a wide margin. Best practice: reach the lake already acclimatized (Arequipa→Colca→Puno→Cusco).","source":"turismoliberty.pe, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the boat trip across the lake dangerous?","a":"Only if you cut corners on the operator. Titicaca is a huge, cold, high-altitude open lake where afternoon wind picks up fast; insist on a licensed lancha with life vests and prefer guided/operator boats over informal transport. Weather can turn quickly on the altiplano.","source":"titicaca.cruises, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lake Titicaca & Puno, Peru — Uros, Taquile & Amantaní Guide, Altitude Tips & Luxury Lodges | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-PE","local_keywords":["Lago Titicaca Uros","islas flotantes Puno","Taquile Amantaní tour","homestay isla Amantaní","chullpas de Sillustani","Virgen de la Candelaria Puno 2026","mal de altura Puno soroche","cómo llegar a Puno desde Cusco","catamarán Lago Titicaca"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"],"primary_keyword":"Lake Titicaca (Puno)","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:51Z","source_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Titilaka (Relais & Châteaux)","location":"Private peninsula near Puno","earning":"Relais & Châteaux / Virtuoso preferred; agency AoR + VIP amenities (upgrade, breakfast, early/late, 50-min massage for two)","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"GHL Hotel Lago Titicaca","location":"Esteves Island","earning":"agency + affiliate; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Casa Andina Premium Puno","location":"Puno lakeshore","earning":"agency + affiliate; agency AoR","mor":"agency/hotel","tier":"$$$"},{"name":"Private catamaran (Peru-side day charter)","location":"Open lake ex-Puno","earning":"lake-operator charter; agency-coordinated","mor":"operator","tier":"$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Lake Titicaca (Puno), Peru, Peru"},"geo":{"lat":-15.8402,"lng":-70.0219},"orbit":[{"id":"arequipa-colca-canyon-peru","jewels":12,"si":["expedition","romance","culture"]},{"id":"lima-peru","jewels":12,"si":["romance","expedition","culinary","culture"]},{"id":"paracas-nazca-peru","jewels":8,"si":["expedition","culture","culinary"]},{"id":"tambopata-amazon-peru","jewels":10,"si":["expedition","wildlife","romance","river"]}],"orbit_country":["cusco-peru","machu-picchu-peru"]}'::jsonb, 57),
  ('lima-peru', '10S', 'Lima', 'Peru', 'The world''s table, on the Pacific', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Lima, South Coast & Amazon', '{"romance","expedition","culinary","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Home to the World''s #1 restaurant 2025 (Maido, Nikkei) plus Central (former #1, Best of the Best), Kjolle #9, Merito #26, Mayta #39 - a global top-tier food capital.","Pre-Inca adobe pyramids inside the modern city (Huaca Pucllana, ~200-700 AD, in Miraflores) alongside the UNESCO colonial Centro Historico and the Convento de San Francisco catacombs.","Jorge Chavez (LIM) is South America''s newest mega-hub: new $2.4B Fraport/LAP terminal opened June 1, 2025 (3x size, up to 40M pax/yr, 46 gates, 2nd runway); the gateway to Cusco/MP, the Amazon, Titicaca and the south coast.","Cool Pacific-desert climate: warm sunny summer Dec-Apr; grey misty ''garua'' winter May-Nov (dry but overcast) - the driest window for Machu Picchu, which drives Lima''s derivative winter spike.","Bohemian Barranco (Puente de los Suspiros) and clifftop Miraflores (Malecon, Costa Verde paragliding) anchor the boutique-romance line; genuine global-flag ultra (Belmond, Relais & Chateaux, LHW, JW Marriott)."],"safety":{"emergency":"105 National Police (PNP) / 106 SAMU medical-ambulance / 116 Bomberos (fire); iPeru tourist assistance (01-574-8000, desks at LIM/Miraflores/Larcomar)","hospital":"Lima has Peru''s best private hospitals/clinics (Clinica Anglo Americana, Ricardo Palma, Clinica Internacional) for stabilization; serious trauma routes to US medical evacuation - carry evac-capable insurance","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Jorge Chavez Intl (LIM), Callao - new Fraport/LAP terminal opened 2025-06-01; SA hub; LIM->Miraflores ~45-60 min via hotel/DMC transfer (not street taxi)","urban_crime_discipline":"stay in Miraflores/Barranco/San Isidro; registered radio-taxi or ride-hail app or hotel transfer only (never unmarked street taxi - express-kidnapping setup); beware distraction theft; in-bank ATMs only; don''t display valuables","state_of_emergency_note":"verify current status live","altitude":"Lima at sea level (no altitude issue; useful soft-landing before Cusco 3,400 m / Titicaca 3,800 m)","dengue":"low on cool Lima coast; higher on Amazon/northern extensions","malaria":"no malaria risk in Lima (highland/coastal capital); Amazon extensions do carry risk - CDC consult for those legs","water":"bottled/purified only (also underpins reputable-cebicheria raw-fish hygiene rule)","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:51Z","page_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00","source_country":"peru","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The VRAEM (Apurimac, Ene and Mantaro valley)","lvl":4},{"name":"The Colombia-border area of Loreto","lvl":4}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"PE","source":"UK FCDO, May 2025","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak_coastal_summer":"Dec-Apr - Lima''s own warm/sunny curve (beaches, nightlife, paragliding, surfing); highest crowds/prices","inflection_gateway_winter":"Jun-Aug - derivative spike as travelers bookend the driest Machu Picchu window through Lima","garua":"May-Nov grey misty sea-fog winter (dry but overcast); sell as culinary/culture bookend, not beach","fire_date":"coastal-summer curve: fire ~mid-November (curve-start -1-2 wks); MP-derivative winter curve: fire ~mid-May; practically, attach Lima nights to whenever the parent Cusco/MP campaign fires","booking_lead":"top tasting menus (Central/Maido/Kjolle) weeks ahead - reservation-first; city hotels 2-3 months for summer; Cusco/Amazon-attached bookends 3-6 months","shoulder":"Apr-May & Sep-Nov (better deals, workable weather)","off_season_specials":"grey-winter ''gastronomy bookend'': tasting-menu circuit, cebicheria lunches, Larco/Pachacamac/San Francisco heritage, cooking classes, pisco-sour masterclasses","event_peaks":["Fiestas Patrias late July (Independence, domestic peak)","Mistura-successor gastronomy festival (name/dates UNVERIFIED - confirm live)","Christmas/New Year (summer)"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Central / Maido / Kjolle tasting menus","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"The world-ranked Lima fine-dining trinity - Maido (World''s #1 2025), Central (Best of the Best), Kjolle (#9); book weeks ahead, reservation-first.","bookable_category":"direct reservation or DMC culinary program","tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.theworlds50best.com/stories/News/maido-lima-the-worlds-best-restaurant-2025.html","si":"culinary","blurb":"The world-ranked Lima fine-dining trinity - Maido (World''s #1 2025), Central (Best of the Best), Kjolle (#9); book weeks ahead, reservation-first.","commission":"DMC culinary-program AOR 10-15%; raw restaurant deposit pass-through","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":15,"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"La Mar cebicheria (Gaston Acurio)","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Acurio''s flagship Miraflores cebicheria (est. 2005), Latin America''s 50 Best - the definitive lunch-only ceviche experience.","bookable_category":"direct / DMC food tour (lunch only)","tier":"premier","source":"http://limacitykings.com/la-mar-cebicheria-peruana/","si":"culinary","blurb":"Acurio''s flagship Miraflores cebicheria (est. 2005), Latin America''s 50 Best - the definitive lunch-only ceviche experience.","commission":"DMC food-program AOR / Viator affiliate 4-8%; walk-in pass-through","wells":["eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Pisco Sour at the Country Club English Bar","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"SUMMUM-award-winning Pisco Sour (2012/2013/2022 best bar in Lima) in the 1927 hotel''s traditional English Bar.","bookable_category":"walk-in / hotel guest","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country_Club_Lima_Hotel","si":"culinary","blurb":"SUMMUM-award-winning Pisco Sour (2012/2013/2022 best bar in Lima) in the 1927 hotel''s traditional English Bar.","commission":"pairs with Country Club stay (hotel AOR); bar spend pass-through","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Huaca Pucllana","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Pre-Inca (~200-700 AD) adobe pyramid in the heart of Miraflores, with an acclaimed on-site restaurant overlooking the floodlit ruin.","bookable_category":"site tour / restaurant","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g294316-d311722-Reviews-Huaca_Pucllana-Lima_Lima_Region.html","si":"culture","blurb":"Pre-Inca (~200-700 AD) adobe pyramid in the heart of Miraflores, with an acclaimed on-site restaurant overlooking the floodlit ruin.","commission":"DMC/affiliate on tour; site fee + restaurant pass-through","wells":["eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary","culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"evidenced","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Convento de San Francisco catacombs","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"1540 Franciscan monastery in the UNESCO Centro Historico with catacombs holding tens of thousands of bones.","bookable_category":"guided city tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","si":"culture","blurb":"1540 Franciscan monastery in the UNESCO Centro Historico with catacombs holding tens of thousands of bones.","commission":"DMC/affiliate 4-10%; entry pass-through","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Larco Museum (Museo Larco)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Pre-Columbian masterpiece collection in an 18th-c. mansion over a pyramid, with a famed garden restaurant; the ''Huacas & Larco by night'' tour is a classic.","bookable_category":"entry / night tour + dinner","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Lima/Huacas-and-Larco-Museum-by-Night-with-Dinner/d928-7465P4","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Pre-Columbian masterpiece collection in an 18th-c. mansion over a pyramid, with a famed garden restaurant; the ''Huacas & Larco by night'' tour is a classic.","when":"year-round","commission":"Viator night-tour affiliate 4-8%; entry pass-through","wells":["stay","eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary","culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"evidenced","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Pachacamac archaeological complex","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Vast pre-Inca/Inca pilgrimage city (pyramids, temples, plazas) ~30 km south of Lima with an on-site museum; easy half-day.","bookable_category":"DMC/Viator day tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Vast pre-Inca/Inca pilgrimage city (pyramids, temples, plazas) ~30 km south of Lima with an on-site museum; easy half-day.","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC 10-12% / affiliate 4-8%; site entry pass-through","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":12,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Callao Monumental street-art district","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Regenerated Callao port-district arts quarter - murals, galleries and design studios in old republican buildings; go with a vetted tour.","bookable_category":"guided art tour (zone awareness)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Regenerated Callao port-district arts quarter - murals, galleries and design studios in old republican buildings; go with a vetted tour.","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/affiliate 4-10%; confirm live tour product + safe corridor","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Barranco + Puente de los Suspiros","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Bohemian seafront district - murals, galleries, the romance-legend Bridge of Sighs and sunset bars; Lima''s honeymoon base.","bookable_category":"self-guided within corridor / guided art walk","tier":"luxury","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","si":"romance","blurb":"Bohemian seafront district - murals, galleries, the romance-legend Bridge of Sighs and sunset bars; Lima''s honeymoon base.","commission":"pairs with Hotel B/Barranco boutique stay (hotel AOR); walk affiliate 4-8%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"evidenced","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["affiliate","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Miraflores Malecon + Parque del Amor at sunset","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Clifftop coastal promenade above the Pacific with the mosaic ''Park of Love'' - the classic Lima romance postcard, free.","bookable_category":"free / paired with clifftop dinner","tier":"essential","source":"https://kaypiperutours.com/must-visit-attractions-in-lima/","si":"romance","blurb":"Clifftop coastal promenade above the Pacific with the mosaic ''Park of Love'' - the classic Lima romance postcard, free.","commission":"bundled into commissionable romance program / dinner","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"evidenced","culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["bundle"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Tandem paragliding off the Miraflores cliffs","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Guided tandem flight over the Costa Verde clifftops and Pacific from the ~80 m Miraflores launch - the signature Lima adventure.","bookable_category":"reputable tandem operator / Viator (guided-only)","tier":"premier","source":"https://pariwana-hostel.com/en/blog/2025/10/07/paragliding-in-lima-a-complete-guide-to-flying-over-the-costa-verde/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided tandem flight over the Costa Verde clifftops and Pacific from the ~80 m Miraflores launch - the signature Lima adventure.","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 10-12%","wells":["fly","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Costa Verde surf lesson","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Guided surf school on the Miraflores/Barranco beach breaks (Makaha/Waikiki); cold-water summer swell, certified instructor + wetsuit.","bookable_category":"surf school / Viator (guided-only)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://pariwana-hostel.com/en/blog/2025/10/07/paragliding-in-lima-a-complete-guide-to-flying-over-the-costa-verde/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided surf school on the Miraflores/Barranco beach breaks (Makaha/Waikiki); cold-water summer swell, certified instructor + wetsuit.","commission":"affiliate 4-8%","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"How do I actually get a table at Maido, Central or Kjolle?","a":"Book weeks ahead — the tables are the binding constraint, not the hotel. Central, Maido and Kjolle open reservations on a rolling monthly/multi-week basis and sell out, so the culinary itinerary must be built reservation-first; grey winter is fine because the dining is indoors.","source":"ohlalima.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What can I see in Lima in a day or two?","a":"More than you''d expect for a gateway city. Walk to Huaca Pucllana (a ~200–700 AD adobe pyramid in Miraflores), the Convento de San Francisco (founded 1540) catacombs in the UNESCO Centro Histórico, and the Larco Museum''s 5,000-year pre-Columbian collection in an 18th-century mansion.","source":"kaypiperutours.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Lima good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — the base is bohemian Barranco, Lima''s most walkable, romantic district, home to the Puente de los Suspiros (\"Bridge of Sighs\") and to Hotel B, a restored 1914 Belle Époque arts-mansion that is the city''s only Relais & Châteaux.","source":"relaischateaux.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Lima?","a":"Urban street crime, not any activity. Stay in Miraflores, Barranco and San Isidro; use only registered radio-taxis, ride-hail apps or hotel transfers — never an unmarked street taxi, the classic express-kidnapping setup (forced ATM withdrawals over 1–3 hours). Use in-bank ATMs and keep valuables out of sight.","source":"bushop.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Lima Peru Travel Guide 2026 — World''s #1 Restaurant, Pre-Inca Ruins & Barranco | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Lima, Peru: the world''s #1 restaurant (Maido), Central, Kjolle and La Mar; pre-Inca Huaca Pucllana, Larco Museum and Pachacamac; bohemian Barranco; luxury Belmond & Relais & Chateaux stays","slug":"lima-peru","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":["en","es-PE"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Lima","mejores restaurantes Lima","Barranco Miraflores","Puente de los Suspiros","tour Huaca Pucllana","Museo Larco","Pachacámac desde Lima","parapente Costa Verde Lima","mejor época para viajar a Lima","cebicherías Lima","pisco sour Lima"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-07","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:51Z","source_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Miraflores Park, A Belmond Hotel","why_ultra":"82-room clifftop Pacific-Riviera flagship in Miraflores; boutique service + full-luxury amenities; Lima''s iconic ultra address and a Belmond = Virtuoso-preferred flag (CLAUDE.md moat)","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or Fora (Amex FHR-listed)","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso-preferred / consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Hotel B","why_ultra":"Lima''s only Relais & Chateaux - restored 1914 Belle Epoque arts-mansion in Barranco, connected to the Lucia de la Puente gallery; the romance/honeymoon ultra pick","earning":"on application / Fora or Relais & Chateaux consortia where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Country Club Lima Hotel","why_ultra":"five-star 1927 San Isidro landmark (California-colonial, national heritage), Leading Hotels of the World; award-winning Perroquet + SUMMUM-winning English Bar Pisco Sour; living-history grandeur","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or Fora / LHW Leaders Club where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"LHW/consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"},{"name":"JW Marriott Hotel Lima","why_ultra":"oceanfront Miraflores tower on the Costa Verde clifftop, steps from Larcomar/Malecon; best-located branded-luxury oceanfront with Bonvoy + STARS/Luminous eligibility","earning":"on application / Marriott STARS/Luminous or Fora where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS/Luminous amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Lima, Peru"},"geo":{"lat":-12.0464,"lng":-77.0428},"orbit":[{"id":"arequipa-colca-canyon-peru","jewels":12,"si":["expedition","romance","culture"]},{"id":"lake-titicaca-puno-peru","jewels":8,"si":["culture"]},{"id":"paracas-nazca-peru","jewels":8,"si":["expedition","culture","culinary"]},{"id":"tambopata-amazon-peru","jewels":10,"si":["expedition","wildlife","romance","river"]}],"orbit_country":["cusco-peru","machu-picchu-peru"]}'::jsonb, 58),
  ('loreto-mexico', '10S', 'Loreto', 'Mexico', 'Blue whales and five empty islands', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"expedition","tropical","diveglobal","romance"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Loreto Bay sheltered by 5 uninhabited islands (Coronado, del Carmen, Danzante, Monserrat, Santa Catalina); marine park w/ 40+ dive/snorkel sites (Source: wildloreto.com, 2026-07-04)","Blue-whale season ~Jan-Mar, strongest early Feb to mid-Mar (Source: thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04)","Humpback, fin, sei whales + dolphins, rays, sea lions, turtles also frequent the bay (Source: thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04)","Whale tours depart Loreto Marina / Marina Puerto Escondido, 4-6 h (Source: sallysees.com, 2026-07-04)","LTO airport served by Alaska/American/Volaris/WestJet; no non-stop LTO-SJD (Source: flightsfrom.com, 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","nearest_trauma":"Loreto clinics for routine; serious trauma/recompression to La Paz (~350 km) or Los Cabos","malaria":"none","dengue":"present in Baja California Sur (Loreto ~2 cases YTD 2026, low); use repellent","water":"bottled/purified","hurricane":"May 15-Nov 30, peak Aug-Oct","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"MX","summary":"The FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named states, cities and border areas of Mexico — listed below in its own words, each with its own exceptions. The Yucatán Peninsula, Mexico City, Baja California Sur and the other main visitor regions carry no FCDO restriction.","source":"UK FCDO — Mexico travel advice, reviewed 2026-07-16 (verbatim snapshot from the research library)","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (whale season; blue whale Feb-Apr; dry mild high season)","shoulder":"May, Oct-Nov","green":"Jun-Sep (hot, hurricane-exposed, best rates)","out_of_season_fill":"summer island-snorkel, kayak, TPC golf packages","fire_date":"early fall (Sep-Oct) for Jan-Mar whale window; summer green-season golf/island campaigns","event_peaks":["Blue Whale Festival (whale season)","US/Canada winter escape peak","Danzante Bay golf invitational (autumn)"],"booking_lead":"3-6 months for whale-season stays + panga slots; resort peak weeks further out"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Blue-whale watching","si":"expedition","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator","name":"Sierra de la Giganta / mission-canyon hike","si":"expedition","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"primary","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator","name":"Isla Coronado snorkel day","si":"tropical","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator","name":"Isla del Carmen / Puerto Balandra snorkel","si":"tropical","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"evidenced","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"resort/operator","name":"Isla Danzante / Danzante Bay","si":"tropical","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"future","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Loreto Bay Marine Park dives (40+ sites)","si":"diveglobal","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"primary","expedition":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"romance","status":"future","tier":"premier","commission":"resort contract","name":"Villa del Palmar spa + Danzante Bay golf escape","si":"romance","wells":["stay","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"diveglobal":"destination","expedition":"destination","romance":"primary","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to see blue whales in Loreto?","a":"Roughly January–March, strongest early February to about mid-March, because that''s when blue whales feed in the bay; gray and humpback come slightly earlier. Tours are 4–6-hour pangas from Loreto Marina or Puerto Escondido — book the short window 3–6 months ahead.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com / sallysees.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What are Loreto''s islands like?","a":"Five uninhabited islands — Coronado, del Carmen, Danzante, Monserrat and Santa Catalina — shelter the bay with turquoise coves, white-sand beaches and a sea-lion colony, all inside a protected marine park with 40+ snorkel/dive sites. Isla Coronado is the classic day trip.","source":"wildloreto.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Loreto good for a golf-and-spa couples escape?","a":"Yes, if you want premier rather than ultra. Villa del Palmar at Danzante Bay has Mexico''s only TPC course (Best Golf Course in Mexico 2020) and a 39,000-sq-ft spa on a secluded bay — position it as a premier golf-and-whale escape, not an Aman-tier ultra.","source":"villadelpalmarloreto.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the diving remote?","a":"Yes — chamber distance is the gatekeeper. Loreto has local clinics for routine care, but a serious dive bend routes ~350 km south to the La Paz chamber (or Los Cabos), so dive conservatively, keep whale-panga trips to licensed no-chase operators, and observe 18–24 h no-fly before the LTO departure.","source":"scubaboard.com / dan.org, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Loreto Mexico — Blue Whales, Marine Park & Island Snorkel | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Loreto, Baja California Sur: blue-whale season, five uninhabited islands, Loreto Bay Marine Park diving, TPC Danzante Bay golf. Pueblo Magico gateway, plan by season.","long_tail":["best time to see blue whales in Loreto","Loreto whale watching tours 2026","Isla Coronado snorkel","TPC Danzante Bay golf","Villa del Palmar Loreto"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["avistamiento de ballena azul Loreto","Parque Nacional Bahia de Loreto","islas de Loreto","buceo Loreto","Pueblo Magico Loreto","tours de ballenas Loreto"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"primary_keyword":["Loreto Mexico","blue whale watching Loreto","Loreto Bay National Park","Loreto islands"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","tropical","diveglobal","romance"],"ultra":[{"what":"Villa del Palmar at the Islands of Loreto by Danzante Bay (premier, not true ultra)","why_ultra":"Mexico''s only TPC course (Rees Jones; Best Golf Course in Mexico 2020), 39,000-sq-ft spa, secluded bay","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso if preferred program exists (verify — not confirmed Virtuoso)","virtuoso_value_add":"resort credit/upgrade where preferred program applies; else standard commission via bedbank/MoR","mor":"resale under resort contract; position as premier golf + whale escape, not Aman/FS-tier ultra; nearest true ultra = Los Cabos/East Cape"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Loreto, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":26.0115,"lng":-111.3486},"orbit":[{"id":"balandra-beach-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["tropical","family","romance"]},{"id":"cabo-pulmo-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","diveglobal"]},{"id":"cabo-san-lucas-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["liveaboard","expedition","ocean","ultra"]},{"id":"east-cape-mexico","jewels":7,"si":["romance","expedition","diveglobal","ocean"]},{"id":"espiritu-santo-island-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","ocean"]},{"id":"la-paz-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","tropical","diveglobal"]},{"id":"l