  ('magdalena-bay-mexico', '10S', 'Magdalena Bay', 'Mexico', 'Gray-whale lagoon, marlin bait-balls', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"expedition","ocean"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Gray-whale breeding lagoon; whales arrive late Dec-early Jan, stay to early/late Apr, peak Jan-Mar (Source: seakayakadventures.com, 2026-07-04)","Famously ''friendly'' gray whales approach boats for close encounters (Source: randomtrip.net, 2026-07-04)","Striped-marlin + sea-lion bait balls form ~mid-Oct-Dec (sardine run) (Source: magdalenabaywhales.com, 2026-07-04)","~5-6 h from Cabo San Lucas, ~3.5-4 h from La Paz; whale towns Puerto San Carlos & Lopez Mateos (Source: randomtrip.net, 2026-07-04)","Lodging is barrier-island glamping camp (~US$650+ 1-night all-in) or basic town hotels — no resorts (Source: thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","nearest_trauma":"basic local care in Puerto San Carlos / Lopez Mateos; serious trauma to La Paz (~3.5-4 h) or Los Cabos (~5-6 h)","malaria":"none","dengue":"present in Baja California Sur; use repellent","water":"bottled/purified","hurricane":"May 15-Nov 30, peak Aug-Oct (whale/marlin windows largely outside peak)","remote_medevac":"remote Pacific coast; barrier-island camp is boat-access only — long ground evac","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}],"fcdo_zones_provenance":{"file":"src/data/safety.json","ref":"f8666636bc25790e0c9643ad5656f8d9fea37bf6","ref_committed":"2026-08-30T05:44:55Z","country_iso2":"MX","summary":"The FCDO advises against all but essential travel to named states, cities and border areas of Mexico — listed below in its own words, each with its own exceptions. The Yucatán Peninsula, Mexico City, Baja California Sur and the other main visitor regions carry no FCDO restriction.","source":"UK FCDO — Mexico travel advice, reviewed 2026-07-16 (verbatim snapshot from the research library)","_rule":"the FCDO restricted-area records for this country, verbatim. PRESENCE OF THIS BLOCK IS NOT A CLAIM THAT THIS DESTINATION SITS IN ANY OF THEM — membership is a coverage judgement and is set only in `zone_record`, by a human."}},"timing":{"peak":"gray-whale HARD window ~mid-Jan-mid-Mar (calving lagoon)","second_peak":"sardine run / striped-marlin bait ball, mid-Oct-Dec","shoulder":"late Dec-early Jan (arrival), late Mar-Apr (tail-end)","green":"May-Sep (off-season, hot, hurricane-exposed)","out_of_season_fill":"minimal; sport fishing + birding fill edges","fire_date":"gray-whale 9-12 months out; marlin/sardine-run by mid-summer for Oct-Dec","event_peaks":["US/Canada winter escape overlaps gray-whale peak"],"booking_lead":"6-12 months (tiny whale-camp capacity, both windows sell out early)"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Gray-whale calving-lagoon encounter","si":"expedition","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"premier","commission":"operator; net-rate red","name":"Barrier-island whale-camp overnight","si":"expedition","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"expedition","status":"live","tier":"essential","commission":"operator","name":"Mangrove / birding skiff","si":"expedition","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","ocean":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"premier","commission":"operator agreement","name":"Snorkel-with-striped-marlin bait ball (sardine run)","si":"ocean","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","ocean":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"luxury","commission":"operator/wholesale","name":"Striped-marlin liveaboard (Nautilus)","si":"ocean","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","ocean":"primary"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is gray-whale season in Magdalena Bay?","a":"The hard window is roughly mid-January to mid-March, when mothers and calves fill the calving lagoon; whales arrive late Dec–early Jan and linger to April. Mag Bay''s grays are famously \"friendly,\" often approaching the pangas — book the tiny whale-camp capacity 6–12 months ahead.","source":"seakayakadventures.com / randomtrip.net, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can I snorkel the striped-marlin bait balls?","a":"Yes, from about mid-October to December — but it''s an advanced open-water activity. You''re offshore in current among fast-moving marlin and sea lions driving sardines to the surface, so it''s for confident, fit snorkelers and freedivers with specialist operators only.","source":"magdalenabaywhales.com / divernet.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Where do I stay — are there resorts?","a":"No resorts — the accurate options are a barrier-island whale camp (glamping, 1–7 nights, ~$650+ for a 1-night all-in) or basic hotels in Puerto San Carlos and López Mateos. The camp is part of the experience: whales from shore, and nothing between you and the lagoon.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is the bait-ball snorkel dangerous?","a":"It is not a beginner activity. The sardine run happens offshore in current among fast predators, so go only with specialist operators, follow the guide''s positioning rules and never touch the wildlife; if you dive elsewhere in Baja, the nearest chambers are La Paz and Cabo San Lucas with 18–24 h no-fly.","source":"divernet.com / sssnetwork.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Magdalena Bay — Gray-Whale Lagoon & Striped-Marlin Sardine Run | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Magdalena Bay, Baja California Sur: gray-whale calving lagoon (Jan-Mar) and the striped-marlin bait-ball sardine run (Oct-Dec). Whale-camp stays, seasons, safe-panga guidance.","long_tail":["gray whale season Magdalena Bay 2026","snorkel with striped marlin Baja","Magdalena Bay whale camp","Puerto San Carlos whale watching","how to get to Magdalena Bay from Los Cabos"],"search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["ballena gris Bahia Magdalena","avistamiento de ballenas Puerto San Carlos","marlin rayado Bahia Magdalena","corrida de la sardina Baja","campamento de ballenas Bahia Magdalena"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristAttraction","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"primary_keyword":["Magdalena Bay whale watching","gray whale Magdalena Bay","striped marlin bait ball","Baja sardine run"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","ocean"],"ultra":[{"what":"National Geographic / Lindblad expedition cruise to Magdalena Bay (sea-based); or Los Cabos/East Cape ultra property as pre/post base","why_ultra":"small-ship expedition w/ naturalists is the only refined product on the bay; no land ultra exists here (nearest = Los Cabos/East Cape 3.5-6 h away)","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso; expedition-cruise lines carry advisor commission","virtuoso_value_add":"shipboard credit/expedition perks via preferred programs, or resort credit at Los Cabos base","mor":"resale via host-Virtuoso / cruise-wholesale only; Magdalena Bay lodging itself is NOT ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Magdalena Bay, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.6167,"lng":-112.1},"orbit":[{"id":"balandra-beach-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["tropical","family","romance"]},{"id":"cabo-pulmo-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","diveglobal"]},{"id":"cabo-san-lucas-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["liveaboard","expedition","ocean","ultra"]},{"id":"east-cape-mexico","jewels":7,"si":["romance","expedition","diveglobal","ocean"]},{"id":"espiritu-santo-island-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","ocean"]},{"id":"la-paz-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","tropical","diveglobal"]},{"id":"loreto-mexico","jewels":7,"si":["expedition","tropical","diveglobal","romance"]},{"id":"los-barriles-mexico","jewels":8,"si":["ocean","expedition","tropical"]},{"id":"san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["romance","expedition","culture","ocean"]},{"id":"todos-santos-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["expedition","culture","wellness","ocean"]}],"orbit_country":["akumal-mexico","bacalar-mexico","calakmul-mexico","campeche-city-mexico","cancun-mexico","careyes-mexico","celestun-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","chichen-itza-mexico","coba-mexico","costalegre-mexico","cozumel-mexico","ensenada-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","holbox-mexico","huatulco-mexico","isla-contoy-mexico","isla-mujeres-mexico","izamal-mexico","mahahual-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","merida-mexico","mexico-city-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","palenque-mexico","playa-del-carmen-mexico","puerto-aventuras-mexico","puerto-mo